<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharaf al-Din Qaraqush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1212</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharaf al-Din Qaraqush was an Armenian-born mamluk who carved out a domain in Tripolitania and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. A follower of Taqi al-Din, nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, he led Turkish and Ghuzz troops west from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> around 1172, seized Tripoli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabes">Gabès</a> and other towns, and allied with the Banu Ghaniya against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>. Repeatedly defeated by Almohad forces, he was driven into the Libyan interior, where he was killed around 1212.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharaf-al-din-qaraqush.jpg" alt="Sharaf al-Din Qaraqush" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: naturalearthdata.com, offered to the Public Domain per Terms of Use Drawing: पाटलिपुत्र (talk) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayyubid_expansion_1174-1193.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
